<h2>Chapter 7: Emergency and After-Hours Marketing</h2>
<p>Emergency HVAC service is where the highest margins live. Emergency rates run $140–$400+ per hour, often doubling or tripling for after-hours calls. But emergency marketing is not about running ads at midnight. It is about building visibility, trust, and infrastructure before the emergency happens.</p>
<h3>The Speed-to-Lead Imperative</h3>
<p>Thirty-five to fifty percent of sales go to the vendor that responds first. In emergency HVAC, that number is even higher.</p>
<div class="cost-table">
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Response Time</th>
<th>Conversion Rate vs. Baseline</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
